<urn:atm:triage:finding/AG18-QA-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AG18-QA-001" ;
  triage:title "Hard Merge Gate LOC failure" ;
  triage:description "docs/plans/phase-AG/sprint-AG18.md Hard Merge Gate requires sprint AG.18 to deliver at least -100 net LOC across crates/ measured as git diff --stat <sprint-base-sha>..HEAD -- crates/. On feature/pAG-s18-unify-envelope-handler @ 70cce097, git diff --stat 03c873fc..70cce097 -- crates/ = 387 insertions(+), 365 deletions(-) = +22 net LOC, the wrong sign relative to the required <= -100 net LOC. Independently verified by quality-mgr, req-qa, and arch-qa. This is a per-sprint numeric merge gate on AG.18's own named-target diff, not a repeatable code pattern; sweep_scope is restricted to feature/pAG-s18-unify-envelope-handler." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "feature/pAG-s18-unify-envelope-handler" ;
  triage:category "merge-gate" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-19T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG18-QA-001/pAG-s18/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s21/56fdcdef> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s21/56fdcdef> ;
  triage:notes "Correlation across the ordered ladder (sprint-base 03c873fc): s18 own-diff (03c873fc..70cce097, crates/) = +22 net LOC, FAILS its own <= -100 gate. Downstream sprints each pass their own independent per-sprint gates: s19 own-diff (70cce097..59225e0f) = 144 insertions/277 deletions = -133 net LOC (PASS); s20 own-diff (59225e0f..50572166) = 104 insertions/622 deletions = -518 net LOC (PASS). Ladder-wide aggregate at s20 tip (03c873fc..50572166, crates/) = 615 insertions/1244 deletions = -629 net LOC, well under -100, so the aggregate reduction requirement is not at risk -- only s18's own per-sprint deliverable is out of compliance. s21 (head 56fdcdef) is only a merge-forward of s20 into s21 with no new dev commits yet (still in progress); it inherits the s18 defect unchanged and has not yet contributed its own diff to evaluate. s22-25 (feature/pAG-s22.. through s25..) are all still pinned at baseline 03c873fc (not started) and have not yet picked up any AG.18-AG.21 commits, so the defect is not yet present there -- note as not-yet-applicable, re-check when those sprints branch forward. Per team fix-dispatch policy (fix dispatch targets latest sprint branch, never integrate; merge-forward closes lower occurrences), promote_to_branch is set to the highest currently-open branch with real commits, feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing @ 56fdcdef. Fix must land as additional deletions against AG.18's named target files (crates/atm-core/src/protocol.rs, crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs, crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs, crates/atm-daemon/src/non_claude_outbound_runtime.rs, crates/atm/src/composition.rs, crates/atm-graft/src/lib.rs, crates/atm-daemon-client/src/rpc.rs, crates/atm-daemon/src/peer_transport.rs) sufficient to bring the s18-attributable portion of the diff to <= -100 net LOC, then merge-forward through s19, s20, s21 to close all occurrences. Re-verify this numeric gate per-branch after the fix lands; do not mark closed on aggregate-ladder numbers alone since the sprint doc gate is per-sprint, not aggregate." .

